\section{What the table shows}{

\strong{Coefficient rows.} One row per coefficient, as for the matching
model without a design: \code{svyglm} as \code{glm}, \code{svyolr} as \code{MASS::polr()}
(with its \code{Thresholds} block, \link{table_regression_ordinal}), \code{svycoxph} as
\code{survival::coxph()} (\link{table_regression_survival}).

\strong{AME.} The Horvitz-Thompson estimator: the mean unit-level effect
weighted by the sampling weights of the analytic sample, with its
variance from the delta method on the design vcov. It is tested on the
same distribution as the coefficient rows. \code{svyolr} gives one effect per
category.

\strong{Counts.} Both are reported: the observed \code{n} and the \verb{Weighted n}
the estimates describe. \code{svycoxph} adds the number of events.
}

